---
import LegalPage from '../../components/LegalPage.astro';

const legalEmail = 'hello@m8tcha.com';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Protocols for Law Enforcement"
  description="How authorized authorities can submit legal requests to M8tcha."
>
  <p>
    This page describes M8tcha's process for responding to valid requests from law-enforcement and
    government authorities. It does not create rights beyond applicable law and does not replace an
    emergency request process.
  </p>

  <h2>Emergency Requests</h2>
  <p>
    If there is an imminent risk of death or serious physical injury, an authorized official should
    email <a href={`mailto:${legalEmail}`}>{legalEmail}</a> with “EMERGENCY REQUEST” in the subject
    line. Include the agency, official name and contact details, the emergency, the information
    requested, and why disclosure is necessary to address the threat. Contact local emergency
    services first where appropriate.
  </p>
  <p>
    We evaluate emergency requests individually and may disclose information when we reasonably
    believe it is necessary to prevent imminent harm and permitted by law. An emergency request is
    not a substitute for legal process.
  </p>

  <h2>Non-Emergency Requests</h2>
  <p>
    Send subpoenas, court orders, warrants, preservation requests, and other formal legal process to{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${legalEmail}`}>{legalEmail}</a>. Requests should identify the issuing authority,
    legal basis, case or reference number, target account or identifiers, requested data, relevant
    date range, and a point of contact. We review requests for validity, scope, and legal authority
    and may object to or narrow requests where appropriate.
  </p>

  <h2>Preservation and Disclosure</h2>
  <p>
    We may preserve records for a legally valid preservation request and for the period required by
    law. We disclose only information responsive to valid process or a lawful emergency request. We
    do not guarantee that requested data exists, is complete, or can be recovered after deletion.
    Account data may be encrypted, aggregated, or held by a service provider and may therefore be
    unavailable to us.
  </p>

  <h2>User Notice</h2>
  <p>
    Where legally permitted, we may notify the affected user before disclosure. We may delay or
    withhold notice when prohibited by law, ordered by a court, or reasonably necessary to prevent
    harm, obstruction, or tampering with an investigation.
  </p>

  <h2>Data Protection and Contact</h2>
  <p>
    We handle government requests consistent with our{' '}
    <a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>{' '}and
    applicable law. We do not accept ordinary customer support, removal, or account-recovery
    requests through this channel. Those requests should be sent to{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${legalEmail}`}>{legalEmail}</a>{' '}with the subject “Support.”
  </p>
</LegalPage>
